proc-self-fd.c: on LikeOS, name a file relative to a directory descriptor
by the path the descriptor was opened with.

Without getxattrat() and its siblings, acl's tools reach a name relative
to a directory descriptor (getfacl -R, setfacl -R, --restore below the
top level) through /proc/self/fd/N/<name>.  On LikeOS /proc/self/fd/N is
a link holding the absolute path the descriptor was opened with, and the
path walk does not cross from /proc into another file system through it.
The link is read instead and the path it holds used (with /<name>
appended).  When it holds no absolute path, the /proc/self/fd path is used
as before.

